card.statement:
Let $\{\phi_n, n\geq0\}$ be a sequence of polynomials (monic) where $p_n$ is a polynomial of degree $n$, satisfying the following recursion

\begin{equation}
\phi_n=(x-\mu_n)\phi_{n-1}-\lambda_n\phi_{n-2},\qquad n=1,2,3,\dots
\end{equation}

for some complex numbers $\mu_n, \lambda_n$, $n=1,2,3,\dots$ and $\phi_{-1}=0$, $\phi_0=1$. Then $\{\phi_n, n\geq 0\}$ is a sequence of orthogonal polynomials with respect to a (unique) weight measure if and only if $\mu_n\in\mathbb R$ and $\lambda_{n+1}>0$ for all $n\ge1$.
